# 26. Concurrency Bugs You Should Recognize

Learn to identify:

### Race condition

```text
Two threads access shared state
without appropriate synchronization.
```

### Deadlock

```text
Threads wait forever.
```

### Livelock

```text
Threads keep responding but don't progress.
```

### Starvation

```text
A thread never gets sufficient resources.
```

### Data race

```text
Concurrent conflicting accesses where at least
one is a write and synchronization requirements
are violated.
```

### Use-after-free

```text
Thread A frees memory
Thread B accesses it
```

### ABA problem

A value changes:

```text
A → B → A
```

A thread may incorrectly think:

```text
"Nothing changed."
```

This becomes important in lock-free algorithms.

---

# 27. Debugging Concurrency

Learn tools and techniques for finding races.

Use:

```text
ThreadSanitizer
```

to detect many data races.

Use:

```text
GDB
```

to inspect:

* Threads
* Stack traces
* Breakpoints
* Thread state

Useful commands include:

```text
info threads
thread <id>
bt
```

Also learn how to reproduce bugs reliably.

Concurrency bugs may happen:

```text
1 / 1000 runs
```

instead of every time.

